(29, 'New Real Estate Article', 'new-real-estate-article-6708', 'New Real Estate Article | Blog Details | FS Real Estate Advisory', 'Write your opening article introduction here...', '{"hero":{"heading":"REAL ESTATE NEWS & INSIGHTS OPPORTUNITY.","mainHeading":"REAL ESTATE NEWS & INSIGHTS OPPORTUNITY.","title":"REAL ESTATE NEWS & INSIGHTS OPPORTUNITY.","tagline":"Expert insights, market analysis, and the latest updates on Dubai\'s thriving real estate market","badge":"Expert insights, market analysis, and the latest updates on Dubai\'s thriving real estate market","titleLine1":"REAL ESTATE","titleLine2":"NEWS & INSIGHTS","titleLine3":"OPPORTUNITY.","subheading":"Expert insights, market analysis, and the latest updates on Dubai\'s thriving real estate market","primaryCtaText":"Start AI Assessment","primaryCtaLink":"\\/ai-assessment","secondaryCtaText":"Browse Opportunities","secondaryCtaLink":"\\/the-valley","backgroundImage":"\\/blog-hero.png","coverImage":"\\/blog-hero.png","bgImage":"\\/blog-hero.png","detailHtml":"<h2>REAL ESTATE <span style=\\"color:#BFA16A\\">NEWS & INSIGHTS<\\/span> OPPORTUNITY.<\\/h2><p>Expert insights, market analysis, and the latest updates on Dubai\'s thriving real estate market<\\/p>"},"customSections":{"blog-hero":{"breadcrumbHome":"Home","breadcrumbCurrent":"Blogs","titleLine1":"bisma 123","titleLine2":"NEWS & INSIGHTS","subheading":"Expert insights, market analysis, and the latest updates on Dubai\'s thriving real estate market","searchPlaceholder":"Looking for Something Specific?","bgImage":"\\/1794379808_1793342026_community.png","headingLine1":"bisma 123","backgroundImage":"\\/1794379808_1793342026_community.png","coverImage":"\\/1794379808_1793342026_community.png"},"blog-content":{"title":"New Real Estate Article","category":"Real Estate","date":"November 11, 2026","tag":"Featured Guide","author":"FS Editorial Advisory","introParagraph":"Write your opening article introduction here...","secondParagraph":"Expand with market analysis, key figures, and investment takeaways...","bodyParagraphs":[]},"blog-images":{"primaryImage":"\\/Rectangle 34625593.png","secondaryImage":"\\/image 299.png"},"blog-keyfigures":{"developer":"EMAAR PROPERTIES","community":"DUBAI HILLS ESTATE","unitTypes":"1, 2 & 3-BEDROOM APARTMENTS","unitSizes":"675 SQ. FT \\u2013 1,777 SQ. FT","startingPrice":"AED 1.2 \\u2013 1.8 MILLION","downPayment":"10%","paymentPlan":"80\\/20","expectedHandover":"2029"},"blog-sidebar":{"categories":[{"label":"Coming Soon","count":6},{"label":"News","count":61},{"label":"Real Estate","count":51}]},"blog-html":{"detailHtml":"<p>Write your opening article introduction here...<\\/p><p>Expand with market analysis, key figures, and investment takeaways...<\\/p>"},"comm-guide":{"detailHtml":"<h2>Off-Plan Properties in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<p>Off-plan property in Dubai refers to the purchase of a new home directly from the developer before construction is complete, typically at a launch price and with a flexible, staged payment plan. It has become the most widely used route into the Dubai real estate market, accounting for roughly three-quarters of all transactions in the emirate, largely because it combines the lowest entry price, instalment-based payments during construction, and strong potential for capital appreciation by the time the project is handed over.<\\/p>\\n<p>Offplans.com lists more than 2,000 live off-plan projects from Dubai\'s leading developers, complete with verified pricing, detailed payment plans, and floor plans, giving investors a single, reliable source to research and compare opportunities across the city.<\\/p>\\n<p>If you are new to off-plan investing, we recommend starting with our complete Off-Plan Dubai Guide, browsing our curated list of off-plan projects in Dubai and off-plan apartments in Dubai, comparing payment plans across developers, or exploring the full catalogue of live off-plan projects currently on the market.<\\/p>\\n\\n<h2>Why Buy Off-Plan Property in Dubai?<\\/h2>\\n<p>Off-plan is the preferred entry point for most investors because it brings together several distinct advantages in a single transaction:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Lower entry price.<\\/strong> Off-plan units are typically priced below comparable ready properties, since developers offer launch-stage pricing to attract early buyers.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Staged payments.<\\/strong> Rather than paying the full purchase price upfront, buyers pay in instalments spread across the construction period, keeping capital available for other investments.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Favourable tax environment.<\\/strong> Dubai imposes no annual property tax, no tax on rental income, and no capital gains tax, allowing investors to retain a greater share of their returns.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Golden Visa eligibility.<\\/strong> A property purchase of AED 2 million or more can qualify the buyer for a 10-year UAE Golden Visa, offering long-term residency benefits.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Escrow-protected payments.<\\/strong> Every off-plan payment is held in a government-regulated escrow account and released to the developer only once construction milestones have been independently certified, ensuring that funds are tied directly to verified progress on site.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>Together these factors make off-plan property one of the most accessible and structurally protected ways to enter the Dubai real estate market, whether for personal use or investment purposes.<\\/p>\\n\\n<h2>How to Buy an Off-Plan Property in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<p>The purchasing process is transparent and well-regulated, and it is open to international buyers with no residency requirement. It generally follows five key stages:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li><strong>Shortlist and compare.<\\/strong> Identify suitable projects based on community, developer reputation, budget, and expected handover date, and compare the available payment plans.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Reserve the unit.<\\/strong> Pay a booking fee and sign the developer\'s reservation form to secure your chosen unit.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Sign the Sales &amp; Purchase Agreement (SPA).<\\/strong> Formalise the purchase and pay the initial down payment, usually between 10% and 20% of the property value.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Register with the Dubai Land Department.<\\/strong> Pay the applicable registration fee and receive your Oqood, the interim title document confirming your ownership during the off-plan period.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Complete the payment plan and take handover.<\\/strong> Continue instalment payments through the construction period, then receive the finished unit along with the full title deed upon completion.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n\\n<h2>Off-Plan vs. Ready Property in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<p>Both off-plan and ready properties have a place in a well-balanced investment strategy, and the right choice depends largely on an investor\'s goals and timeline.<\\/p>\\n<p>A ready property generates rental income immediately and allows buyers to inspect the exact unit before purchase, but it typically requires a larger upfront payment and comes at a higher overall price point. An off-plan property, by contrast, trades that immediate income for a lower entry cost, a longer and more manageable payment schedule, and the opportunity for the property\'s value to appreciate before the buyer even takes possession.<\\/p>\\n<p>Many experienced investors in Dubai use both strategies in tandem \\u2014 allocating capital to off-plan projects to build a growing portfolio over time, while relying on ready units to maintain steady rental cash flow. We encourage you to browse our full range of off-plan projects to compare current prices, developers, and payment structures side by side.<\\/p>\\n\\n<h2>Popular Off-Plan Areas in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Dubai Marina<\\/li>\\n<li>Business Bay<\\/li>\\n<li>Downtown Dubai<\\/li>\\n<li>Dubai Creek Harbour<\\/li>\\n<li>Dubai Hills Estate<\\/li>\\n<li>Jumeirah Village Circle (JVC)<\\/li>\\n<li>Dubai South<\\/li>\\n<li>Palm Jumeirah<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<h2>Leading Off-Plan Developers in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Emaar<\\/li>\\n<li>DAMAC<\\/li>\\n<li>Sobha<\\/li>\\n<li>Binghatti<\\/li>\\n<li>Nakheel<\\/li>\\n<li>Danube<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>"}},"blogMeta":{"blogId":1794379796708,"category":"Real Estate","date":"November 11, 2026","author":"FS Editorial Advisory","imageSrc":"\\/Rectangle 34625593.png"},"metaKeywords":null,"ogImage":"\\/buy_hero.png","featureBar":[{"id":"ai-advisory","title":"AI Advisory Engine","description":"Personalized recommendations based on your goals.","icon":"\\/ai.png"},{"id":"fs-scores","title":"FS Advisory Scores","description":"Proprietary rating across 10+ key factors.","icon":"\\/fs score.png"},{"id":"curated-oppo","title":"Curated Opportunities","description":"Only opportunities that meet our advisory standards.","icon":"\\/curated oppo.png"},{"id":"expert-guidance","title":"Expert Guidance","description":"Human expertise at every step of your journey.","icon":"\\/exp guidance.png"}],"featureBarDetail":"<h3>Advisory &amp; Feature Bar<\\/h3><p>Proprietary algorithms and seasoned real estate advisors deliver tailored opportunities.<\\/p>","featureBarBgImage":"\\/dubai hills.png","opportunities":{"title":"Opportunities We Currently Recommend","heading":"Opportunities We Currently Recommend","titleLine1":"Opportunities We","titleLine2":"Currently Recommend","tagline":"FEATURED INVESTMENTS","badge":"FEATURED INVESTMENTS","description":"Hand-picked, high-yield developments across prime UAE communities.","contentText":"Hand-picked, high-yield developments across prime UAE communities.","viewAllLink":"\\/project-main-page","cards":[{"id":"1","title":"The Valley","developer":"By Emaar","score":92,"tag":"FAMILY LIVING","bestFor":"Growing Families","price":"AED 1.6M","image":"\\/thevalley.png"},{"id":"2","title":"Grand Polo Club & Resort","developer":"By Emaar","score":89,"tag":"LUXURY LIVING","bestFor":"Luxury Lifestyle","price":"AED 4.2M","image":"\\/grandpolo_club.png"},{"id":"3","title":"Dubai Hills Estate","developer":"By Emaar","score":87,"tag":"FAMILY LIVING","bestFor":"End Users & Investors","price":"AED 1.8M","image":"\\/dubai hills.png"}]},"community":{"heading":"Explore by Community","tagline":"FEATURED DISTRICTS","badge":"FEATURED DISTRICTS","description":"Discover master-planned developments and luxury waterfront neighborhoods.","contentText":"Discover master-planned developments and luxury waterfront neighborhoods.","items":[{"name":"Dubai Hills Estate","icon":"\\/dubai_hills.png","href":"#"},{"name":"The Valley","icon":"\\/valleyicon.png","href":"\\/the-valley"},{"name":"Dubai Creek Harbour","icon":"\\/creekicon.png","href":"#"},{"name":"The Oasis","icon":"\\/oasisicon.png","href":"#"},{"name":"Palm Jumeirah","icon":"\\/palmjumeriah icon.png","href":"#"},{"name":"Arabian Ranches III","icon":"\\/arabian 3 icon.png","href":"#"}]},"longContent":{"detailHtml":"<h2>Off-Plan Properties in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<p>Off-plan property in Dubai refers to the purchase of a new home directly from the developer before construction is complete, typically at a launch price and with a flexible, staged payment plan. It has become the most widely used route into the Dubai real estate market, accounting for roughly three-quarters of all transactions in the emirate, largely because it combines the lowest entry price, instalment-based payments during construction, and strong potential for capital appreciation by the time the project is handed over.<\\/p>\\n<p>Offplans.com lists more than 2,000 live off-plan projects from Dubai\'s leading developers, complete with verified pricing, detailed payment plans, and floor plans, giving investors a single, reliable source to research and compare opportunities across the city.<\\/p>\\n<p>If you are new to off-plan investing, we recommend starting with our complete Off-Plan Dubai Guide, browsing our curated list of off-plan projects in Dubai and off-plan apartments in Dubai, comparing payment plans across developers, or exploring the full catalogue of live off-plan projects currently on the market.<\\/p>\\n\\n<h2>Why Buy Off-Plan Property in Dubai?<\\/h2>\\n<p>Off-plan is the preferred entry point for most investors because it brings together several distinct advantages in a single transaction:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Lower entry price.<\\/strong> Off-plan units are typically priced below comparable ready properties, since developers offer launch-stage pricing to attract early buyers.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Staged payments.<\\/strong> Rather than paying the full purchase price upfront, buyers pay in instalments spread across the construction period, keeping capital available for other investments.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Favourable tax environment.<\\/strong> Dubai imposes no annual property tax, no tax on rental income, and no capital gains tax, allowing investors to retain a greater share of their returns.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Golden Visa eligibility.<\\/strong> A property purchase of AED 2 million or more can qualify the buyer for a 10-year UAE Golden Visa, offering long-term residency benefits.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Escrow-protected payments.<\\/strong> Every off-plan payment is held in a government-regulated escrow account and released to the developer only once construction milestones have been independently certified, ensuring that funds are tied directly to verified progress on site.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>Together these factors make off-plan property one of the most accessible and structurally protected ways to enter the Dubai real estate market, whether for personal use or investment purposes.<\\/p>\\n\\n<h2>How to Buy an Off-Plan Property in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<p>The purchasing process is transparent and well-regulated, and it is open to international buyers with no residency requirement. It generally follows five key stages:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li><strong>Shortlist and compare.<\\/strong> Identify suitable projects based on community, developer reputation, budget, and expected handover date, and compare the available payment plans.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Reserve the unit.<\\/strong> Pay a booking fee and sign the developer\'s reservation form to secure your chosen unit.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Sign the Sales &amp; Purchase Agreement (SPA).<\\/strong> Formalise the purchase and pay the initial down payment, usually between 10% and 20% of the property value.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Register with the Dubai Land Department.<\\/strong> Pay the applicable registration fee and receive your Oqood, the interim title document confirming your ownership during the off-plan period.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Complete the payment plan and take handover.<\\/strong> Continue instalment payments through the construction period, then receive the finished unit along with the full title deed upon completion.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n\\n<h2>Off-Plan vs. Ready Property in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<p>Both off-plan and ready properties have a place in a well-balanced investment strategy, and the right choice depends largely on an investor\'s goals and timeline.<\\/p>\\n<p>A ready property generates rental income immediately and allows buyers to inspect the exact unit before purchase, but it typically requires a larger upfront payment and comes at a higher overall price point. An off-plan property, by contrast, trades that immediate income for a lower entry cost, a longer and more manageable payment schedule, and the opportunity for the property\'s value to appreciate before the buyer even takes possession.<\\/p>\\n<p>Many experienced investors in Dubai use both strategies in tandem \\u2014 allocating capital to off-plan projects to build a growing portfolio over time, while relying on ready units to maintain steady rental cash flow. We encourage you to browse our full range of off-plan projects to compare current prices, developers, and payment structures side by side.<\\/p>\\n\\n<h2>Popular Off-Plan Areas in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Dubai Marina<\\/li>\\n<li>Business Bay<\\/li>\\n<li>Downtown Dubai<\\/li>\\n<li>Dubai Creek Harbour<\\/li>\\n<li>Dubai Hills Estate<\\/li>\\n<li>Jumeirah Village Circle (JVC)<\\/li>\\n<li>Dubai South<\\/li>\\n<li>Palm Jumeirah<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<h2>Leading Off-Plan Developers in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Emaar<\\/li>\\n<li>DAMAC<\\/li>\\n<li>Sobha<\\/li>\\n<li>Binghatti<\\/li>\\n<li>Nakheel<\\/li>\\n<li>Danube<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>","backgroundImage":null},"offPlanGuide":{"detailHtml":"<h2>Off-Plan Properties in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<p>Off-plan property in Dubai refers to the purchase of a new home directly from the developer before construction is complete, typically at a launch price and with a flexible, staged payment plan. It has become the most widely used route into the Dubai real estate market, accounting for roughly three-quarters of all transactions in the emirate, largely because it combines the lowest entry price, instalment-based payments during construction, and strong potential for capital appreciation by the time the project is handed over.<\\/p>\\n<p>Offplans.com lists more than 2,000 live off-plan projects from Dubai\'s leading developers, complete with verified pricing, detailed payment plans, and floor plans, giving investors a single, reliable source to research and compare opportunities across the city.<\\/p>\\n<p>If you are new to off-plan investing, we recommend starting with our complete Off-Plan Dubai Guide, browsing our curated list of off-plan projects in Dubai and off-plan apartments in Dubai, comparing payment plans across developers, or exploring the full catalogue of live off-plan projects currently on the market.<\\/p>\\n\\n<h2>Why Buy Off-Plan Property in Dubai?<\\/h2>\\n<p>Off-plan is the preferred entry point for most investors because it brings together several distinct advantages in a single transaction:<\\/p>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Lower entry price.<\\/strong> Off-plan units are typically priced below comparable ready properties, since developers offer launch-stage pricing to attract early buyers.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Staged payments.<\\/strong> Rather than paying the full purchase price upfront, buyers pay in instalments spread across the construction period, keeping capital available for other investments.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Favourable tax environment.<\\/strong> Dubai imposes no annual property tax, no tax on rental income, and no capital gains tax, allowing investors to retain a greater share of their returns.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Golden Visa eligibility.<\\/strong> A property purchase of AED 2 million or more can qualify the buyer for a 10-year UAE Golden Visa, offering long-term residency benefits.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Escrow-protected payments.<\\/strong> Every off-plan payment is held in a government-regulated escrow account and released to the developer only once construction milestones have been independently certified, ensuring that funds are tied directly to verified progress on site.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n<p>Together these factors make off-plan property one of the most accessible and structurally protected ways to enter the Dubai real estate market, whether for personal use or investment purposes.<\\/p>\\n\\n<h2>How to Buy an Off-Plan Property in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<p>The purchasing process is transparent and well-regulated, and it is open to international buyers with no residency requirement. It generally follows five key stages:<\\/p>\\n<ol>\\n<li><strong>Shortlist and compare.<\\/strong> Identify suitable projects based on community, developer reputation, budget, and expected handover date, and compare the available payment plans.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Reserve the unit.<\\/strong> Pay a booking fee and sign the developer\'s reservation form to secure your chosen unit.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Sign the Sales &amp; Purchase Agreement (SPA).<\\/strong> Formalise the purchase and pay the initial down payment, usually between 10% and 20% of the property value.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Register with the Dubai Land Department.<\\/strong> Pay the applicable registration fee and receive your Oqood, the interim title document confirming your ownership during the off-plan period.<\\/li>\\n<li><strong>Complete the payment plan and take handover.<\\/strong> Continue instalment payments through the construction period, then receive the finished unit along with the full title deed upon completion.<\\/li>\\n<\\/ol>\\n\\n<h2>Off-Plan vs. Ready Property in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<p>Both off-plan and ready properties have a place in a well-balanced investment strategy, and the right choice depends largely on an investor\'s goals and timeline.<\\/p>\\n<p>A ready property generates rental income immediately and allows buyers to inspect the exact unit before purchase, but it typically requires a larger upfront payment and comes at a higher overall price point. An off-plan property, by contrast, trades that immediate income for a lower entry cost, a longer and more manageable payment schedule, and the opportunity for the property\'s value to appreciate before the buyer even takes possession.<\\/p>\\n<p>Many experienced investors in Dubai use both strategies in tandem \\u2014 allocating capital to off-plan projects to build a growing portfolio over time, while relying on ready units to maintain steady rental cash flow. We encourage you to browse our full range of off-plan projects to compare current prices, developers, and payment structures side by side.<\\/p>\\n\\n<h2>Popular Off-Plan Areas in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Dubai Marina<\\/li>\\n<li>Business Bay<\\/li>\\n<li>Downtown Dubai<\\/li>\\n<li>Dubai Creek Harbour<\\/li>\\n<li>Dubai Hills Estate<\\/li>\\n<li>Jumeirah Village Circle (JVC)<\\/li>\\n<li>Dubai South<\\/li>\\n<li>Palm Jumeirah<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>\\n\\n<h2>Leading Off-Plan Developers in Dubai<\\/h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Emaar<\\/li>\\n<li>DAMAC<\\/li>\\n<li>Sobha<\\/li>\\n<li>Binghatti<\\/li>\\n<li>Nakheel<\\/li>\\n<li>Danube<\\/li>\\n<\\/ul>","backgroundImage":null},"reviews":{"heading":"What Our Clients Say","tagline":"FROM CLIENT TESTIMONIALS","introText":"Verified experiences from global investors and residents who achieved their real estate goals with FS Advisory.","items":[{"id":"1","name":"Omer Khan","role":"Verified Client","content":"I was looking at the real estate market of Dubai and got in contact with Ms. Hana Taghdis of FS Advisory. She showed me multiple projects and finally I was able to select a unit of my choice.","rating":1},{"id":"2","name":"Nathalie Syvak","role":"Verified Client","content":"Our real estate agent is Yulia Kravchenko, we are very pleased with her work and I would like to note her approach to the client.","rating":3},{"id":"3","name":"Mike Mike","role":"Verified Client","content":"Ultimate admiration! I wanted to know more about the real estate business in Dubai. God sent me a unique intelligent young lady Yulia Kravchenko.","rating":3}],"detailHtml":"<h2>What Our <span style=\\"color:#BFA16A\\">Clients Say<\\/span><\\/h2><p>Verified experiences from global investors and residents.<\\/p>","backgroundImage":"\\/thevalley.png"},"faqs":{"heading":"Frequently Asked Questions","tagline":"UAE off-plan property \\u00b7 Buyer guide","mainHeading":"Everything you need to know about UAE off-plan property","contentText":"Answers To The Questions We Hear Most From People Exploring An Off-Plan Purchase In The UAE \\u2014 From How The Process Works To Ownership, Payment Plans, And What To Check Before You Commit.","items":[{"id":"faq-1","question":"What Does \\"Off-Plan\\" Actually Mean?","answer":"Off-plan property is real estate purchased before it is fully constructed. Buyers invest directly from developers at launch pricing with structured milestone-based installment plans."},{"id":"faq-2","question":"How Do Off-Plan Payment Plans Typically Work?","answer":"Payment plans are structured schedules spread across the construction timeline, typically 10-20% down payment and installments tied to construction milestones."},{"id":"faq-3","question":